  "id": "COMPOUND:295 - PROTEIN:5115",
  "verbalization": "Mitomycin is linked to LS-1034 through a series of molecular interactions involving 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which acts as a target for multiple entities. The evidence suggests that mitomycin targets 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets LS-1034. This implies a potential pathway where mitomycin influences the activity of this compound, which then affects LS-1034. The presence of multiple targets for 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, including both ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5 and histone acetyltransferase KAT8, suggests a broader role in cellular processes that could be modulated by mitomycin. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which mitomycin exerts its effects on LS-1034, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
